<Project>
  <!-- Deliberately does NOT import the repo-root Directory.Build.props. MSBuild walks up and
       stops at the FIRST Directory.Build.props it finds, so this shields the IAP-015
       same-account second-session harness from the root's SbprValidateSdkPaths target (which
       hard-errors unless the Valheim managed-assembly path is set).

       UNLIKE tests/ and qa-operator-harness/ (which LINK-COMPILE shipped SOURCE), this harness
       deliberately REFERENCE-LINKS the COMPILED, shipped admission assemblies
       (SBPR.Niflheim.HomesteadStones.dll + SBPR.Trailborne.Core.dll) — the exact-binary
       production-identical requirement of AT-AIP-DEDICATED-SECOND-SESSION-REJECT (Option B,
       architect DECIDE t_13db2c95). A re-implemented or source-recompiled admission core does
       NOT satisfy this AT. The harness self-attests: at runtime it SHA-256-hashes the assembly
       file it actually loaded the admission types from and prints it as evidence, so the proof
       is provably against the linked binary, not a parallel copy. -->
</Project>
